 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Trump announced an energy truce. Then a power plant burned. Did Russia agree?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Sunday, Trump posted that Russia and Ukraine agreed to an immediate energy ceasefire. His post gave no details. It ended: Do not break it. Zelenskyy said he first heard about it from the media."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Hours later, Ukraine says Russia hit a power plant in Kharkiv, and gas sites of the state company Naftogaz. Zelenskyy says Russia carried out more than two hundred strikes on Ukraine's power system this week. Those are Ukrainian claims."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Kyiv says it will pause if Moscow does. The Kremlin would not say whether it agreed. Spokesman Dmitry Peskov said only, contacts are ongoing. The Associated Press notes Trump announced a similar deal before. It did not hold."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will both sides stop hitting energy sites before winter? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
